            <div xml:id="d287">

                <pb facs="0376" n="274" sameAs="frus:frus1933v03/pg274"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">793.94/6174: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in China (Johnson) to the Secretary of
                        State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Peiping</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1933-04-12T13:00:00+08:00">April 12, 1933—1
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received April 12—12:45 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>321. Following from American Consul General at Mukden: <quote rend="blockquote">
                        <p>“April 11, 8 p.m. Army spokesman announced: <list>
                                <label>1.</label>
                                <item>That general attack along the Wall has been in progress since
                                    April 10th in order definitely to suppress Chinese
                                    counterattacks.</item>
                                <label>2.</label>
                                <item>That Lengkou was captured this morning and that Japanese are
                                    advancing toward Chienchangying.</item>
                                <label>3.</label>
                                <item>That aeroplanes bombarded Chinese base of operations at
                                    Dolonor.”</item>
                            </list></p>
                    </quote></p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Johnson</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
